# Salary And Payment Domain Rules

- This assessment manages salary records and insights; do not add real payroll execution unless explicitly requested.
- Represent money with decimal-safe types, never floating point.
- Validate salary ranges and required employee fields at API boundaries.
- Avoid logging full salary payloads, raw request bodies, or sensitive employee details.
- If future payment execution is added, require idempotency keys, immutable ledger entries, reconciliation, authorization, and audit trails.
- Do not overwrite salary values without explicit update intent from the user.
- Keep compensation calculations deterministic and test them with fixed fixtures.
- Return user-friendly validation errors while keeping internal error details out of API responses.
- Treat currency conversion, tax, bonuses, and payroll rules as out of scope unless requirements are formally updated.
- Document any compensation-domain assumption in requirements, architecture notes, or API docs.
